      "math_academy_id": "q-8174",
      "knowledge_point_id": "22d992a1-2ea8-5226-9971-188447f98ab6",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing a Higher-Degree Taylor Polynomial Of a Given Function About a Given Point",
      "problem": "Find the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x$ about $x=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\n{P}_{4}(x)=f(a)+{f}^{\u2032}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{\u2033}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{\u2034}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^{4}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $a=1,$ so\n\n$$\n{P}_{4}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{\u2032}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{\u2033}(1)}{2!}{(x-1)}^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{\u2034}(1)}{3!}{(x-1)}^{3}+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(1)}{4!}{(x-1)}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo we need to work out $f(1),$ ${f}^{\u2032}(1),$ ${f}^{\u2033}(1),$ ${f}^{\u2034}(1)$ and ${f}^{(4)}(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x & \u27f9 &  & f(1) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20611=0 \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{1}{x}={x}^{-1} & \u27f9 &  & {f}^{\u2032}(1) & ={1}^{-1}=1 \\\\ {f}^{\u2033}(x) & =-{x}^{-2} & \u27f9 &  & {f}^{\u2033}(1) & =-(1)^{-2}=-1 \\\\ {f}^{\u2034}(x) & =-(-2){x}^{-3}=2{x}^{-3} & \u27f9 &  & {f}^{\u2034}(1) & =2(1)^{-3}=2 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =2(-3){x}^{-4}=-6{x}^{-4} & \u27f9 &  & {f}^{(4)}(1) & =-6(1)^{-4}=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${P}_{4}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x) & =0+(x-1)-\\frac{1}{2!}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{2}{3!}(x-1)^{3}-\\frac{6}{4!}(x-1)^{4} \\\\  & =(x-1)-\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(x-1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(x-1)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
